{"title":"Career Roadmap · Wearable Tech Engineer","role":"Wearable Tech Engineer","summary":"A Wearable Tech Engineer designs, develops, tests and improves electronic and software systems worn on or integrated into the human body. In sports technology, the focus is on measuring movement, biomechanics, physiological signals, performance and environmental conditions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Sports Engineering / Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Wearable Tech Engineer designs, develops, tests and improves electronic and software systems worn on or integrated into the human body. In sports technology, the focus is on measuring movement, biomechanics, physiological signals, performance and environmental conditions."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical products include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Smartwatches"},{"text":"Fitness trackers"},{"text":"Sports performance sensors"},{"text":"Smart clothing"},{"text":"Smart footwear"},{"text":"GPS sports devices"},{"text":"Heart-rate monitors"},{"text":"Athlete monitoring systems"},{"text":"Motion-tracking devices"},{"text":"Wearable rehabilitation systems"},{"text":"IMU-based biomechanics systems"},{"text":"Wearable medical/sports sensors"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong profile combines:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sports Engineering","Electronics","Embedded Systems","Sensors","Wearable Computing","Biomechanics","Signal Processing","IoT","Data Analytics","Human Factors"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech/B.E. foundation"},{"text":"Electronics, biomechanics, sensors, embedded systems and sports science"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Wearable Tech Engineer"},{"text":"Sensor integration, embedded firmware, data acquisiti